k","quote":"when you were in the garage building your computer and programming them"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"this the perfect opportunity to show you and everyone else what i am capable of"}],"uncertainty":"medium"},{"criterionId":"conventions","observation":"Your essay has a few consistent conventions issues. The pronoun 'I' should always be capitalized, and it appears in lowercase several times. 'Windows' is a proper noun and should be capitalized. Some sentences run together without punctuation, and a few sentences need commas, such as after introductory phrases and before 'such as' lists. Starting each sentence with a capital letter, including after a period, would also make the text easier to read.","suggestedLevel":"l2","excerpts":[{"artifact":"work","quote":"When you created the windows PC"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"Giving me this chance not only helps me but it helps my family and my community. we live in a small town"},{"artifact":"work","quote":"I want the people in my town to experience the wonders of technology i want to show them"}],"uncertainty":"medium"}]}
